# THIS REPO HAS A PUBLIC REMOTE (github.com/PaperTyger/crows-makings).
# Anything committed here can end up on the open web via GitHub Pages.
#
# Added 2026-07-28 after a near-miss: an unreviewed draft section-note --
# outbound text that named Tyson and recounted him correcting me -- was written
# into pieces/ because that is where site content lives. It was never committed,
# but the nightly crows-makings-sync task is instructed to "commit, then push,"
# and a blanket `git add -A` would have swept it onto the public site
# unreviewed. Exactly the failure Standing Audience exists to prevent, and the
# same shape as Click publishing a private remark to a public TODO.md.
#
# Drafts now live in F:\Papyrus\SiteDrafts\ (private, no remote). This pattern
# is the backstop for the day someone forgets that.
